{"topicSections":[{"title":"Making a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"],"anchor":"Making-a-plan"},{"title":"Writing a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files(carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"],"anchor":"Writing-a-plan"},{"title":"Checking a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference"],"anchor":"Checking-a-plan"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplans"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A tracking plan is the contract between an app and whoever reads its events: dashboards, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"warehouse, a collector, another platform’s client. Each event’s document gives its version,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent category, properties and their JSON types, which ones every payload holds, and which are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in a form that needs no Swift to read. Committed beside the events, it puts every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change to them in the pull request as a JSON diff. Its check says which changes break what has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already shipped: payloads from installed app versions that a validating collector would reject,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and stored records the app could no longer decode.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" turns events’ schemas into files: an index, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracking-plan.json"},{"type":"text","text":", and for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event a JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) document and an example payload. The files are values, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same schemas give the same bytes on every run and platform, ready to commit for the people and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tools outside the app."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Checking compares the plan the events make now with the committed one by what the files mean. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a match, a plan that is only out of date, or one with a breaking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"difference: a change that, at the same version, would leave a stored record or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already-released app’s payload unable to decode or validate. Each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event, the property and the change, and says whether it is breaking.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only code compiled against the app’s event types can read their schemas, so the app writes a small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executable of its own: a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"},{"text":", marked ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@main"},{"text":". It writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the plan to a directory, or checks it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"text":". To run the check from the app’s tests instead,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanTesting"},{"text":". The schemas usually come from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"text":"):","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init()"},{"text":" takes every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" in the program and the library’s own events, found at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run time, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init(schemas:)"},{"text":" takes a list.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is a product of its own that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()  \/\/ every @Event in the program, and the library's own","let check = plan.check(against: plan.files)  \/\/ .matches","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", ..., \"signed_up.v1.schema.json\", \"signed_up.v1.example.json\"]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers the executable, the command plugins and the test."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlans"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"TrackingPlans","role":"collection","externalID":"TrackingPlans","symbolKind":"module"},"references":{"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlanCheck":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackingPlanCheck"}],"title":"TrackingPlanCheck","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplancheck","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What checking a tracking plan against the committed one found: a match, a committed plan that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is only out of date, or differences that break it."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackingPlanCheck"}]},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlanCommand":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/Trackin